  "header": "Agents move into everyday work while proof, privacy and control become the real tests",
  "friendlyHeader": "AI can do more, but we still need proof and control",
  "summary": "Today’s issue follows AI from personal errands and enterprise deployment to mathematics, genomics and creative work. The useful thread is not simply greater capability: it is whether actions can be checked, access can be controlled, and results can be measured rather than inferred from activity.",
  "friendlySummary": "Today we look at AI that can handle personal tasks, help companies, study DNA, make images and work on difficult maths. The main lesson is simple: useful AI needs clear permissions, results we can check and honest measures of whether it helped.",
